                <pb facs="0635" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg507"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 357.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21, 1885</date>.
                        (Received April 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 726.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 712, dated
                    February 4, 1885, I, have the honor to advise the Department that on the 13th
                    instant Mr. Eugene V. Garrido was paid by me $2,000, the sum collected from the
                    Haytian Government for personal injury done him on the 22d and 23d days of
                    September, 1883.</p>
                <p>His receipt for the sum named is on file in this legation.</p>
                <p>His satisfaction and thanks, in view of the action and success had in his case,
                    are thorough and cordial.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
